    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our premier asset with an elite efficiency score of 81.88. He benefits from an ideal confluence of variables: a favorable matchup against Avila (4.91 xERA) and a massive 16% park boost, further bolstered by his lead-off role. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (79.36) is a must-start against Sears. While Sears is a lefty, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**\u2019s dynamic platoon edge and favorable spot in the two-hole make him a high-floor, high-ceiling play. Both **Kyle Tucker** (75.35) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) also clear the 75-point threshold; **Jackson Merrill** specifically thrives today due to a significant SP skill advantage (19% boost) against a vulnerable Bieber.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Dominic Smith**, who posted a respectable 50.40 but ultimately fell short due to his lower position in the lineup and superior efficiency numbers offered by **Miguel Vargas** (63.96) and **Josh Lowe** (68.22). **Miguel Vargas** is a high-upside play today, sporting an elite xwOBA of 0.402, which justifies his utility spot despite the lefty-on-lefty matchup against Lopez. While **Heliot Ramos** (50.54) and **Brayan Rocchio** (49.93) are technically \"strong\" or \"marginal\" plays, they are bolstered by their potential for stolen bases\u2014a critical priority for the Waves. We are keeping a close watch on **Heliot Ramos** and **Josh Lowe** for their stolen base potential, as both face pitchers with high-tolerance delivery windows that should facilitate aggressive baserunning.\n\nRisks remain focused on the lower end of our starting rotation. **Sam Antonacci** (58.96) is facing a difficult L/L platoon disadvantage against Lopez, which creates volatility despite his strong batting order position. Furthermore, while we aren't tracking any immediate weather postponements, owners should monitor the wind in matchups involving **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jackson Merrill**, as shifting conditions could impact the park factors that currently pad their high efficiency scores. For those holding players like **Jacob Wilson** or **Nasim Nunez** on the bench, keep them ready; if mid-game substitutions are required, their profiles suggest they are capable of immediate impact should a starter face an injury or a late-inning defensive replacement.",
